        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinton%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Wyoming House, a historic frame house built between the 18th and early 19th centuries, is listed on the Maryland Inventory of Historical Properties.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Clinton%2C_Maryland",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Surratt House Museum, once Mary Surratt’s tavern, now tells the story of Lincoln’s assassination conspirators.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
